        'ECL results' => [
            'body' => '<p>The <b>Expected Credit Loss Management</b> screen lists what the calculation produced, loan by loan, and lets you export it. Open the sidebar, expand <b>ECL Processing</b> and choose <b>ECL Calculation</b>.</p><h4>What you see on the screen</h4><ul><li>Four buttons across the header. <b>Projection Audit</b> opens the time-phased projection evidence. <b>Calculate ECL</b> starts a new run. <b>ECL Reconciliation</b> opens a modal that takes you to the movement report. <b>Export Report</b> opens the export modal.</li><li>Two measurement-basis tabs: <b>Discounted ECL (EIR present value)</b> and <b>Undiscounted ECL</b>. The tab you choose changes the three summary cards and which columns the table shows.</li><li>Three summary cards. On the discounted tab they read <b>Records discounted</b> (with the count of records in the filtered population), <b>Discounted ECL</b>, and <b>Discounting effect</b>, which is the reduction that applying present value produced. On the undiscounted tab they read <b>Records calculated</b>, <b>Undiscounted ECL</b> and <b>ECL coverage of exposure</b>, which is the ECL divided by the carrying exposure.</li><li>An amber banner appears on the discounted tab when some records could not be discounted, telling you how many and asking you to review their discount status, approved EIR and remaining horizon.</li><li>A collapsible <b>Filters</b> panel, headed "Year, month, stage and contract or customer search", with <b>Show filters</b> and <b>Hide filters</b>. The stage list offers All Stages, Stage 1, Stage 2 and Stage 3.</li><li>The results table. Columns are <b>Contract ID</b>, <b>Reporting Period</b>, <b>IFRS Stage</b>, <b>EAD (MWK)</b>, <b>PD</b>, <b>LGD</b>, <b>Undiscounted ECL (MWK)</b> and <b>ECL Coverage</b>. On the discounted tab you also see <b>Original EIR</b>, <b>Discount Horizon (Months)</b>, <b>Discounted ECL (MWK)</b>, <b>Discounting Effect (MWK)</b> and <b>Discount Status</b>. The last column is <b>Updated</b>.</li><li><b>Original EIR</b> shows the solved effective annual rate as a percentage, and the basis beside it tells you where the rate came from. There are four values: <b>Fixed, original</b> means the contract is fixed rate and the original rate applies; <b>Floating, original as proxy</b> means the contract floats but no reset history has been recorded, so the original rate stands in and is labelled as a proxy; <b>Calculated, not approved</b> means a rate was solved but nobody has approved and locked it, so it is not used; <b>No EIR</b> means no rate exists for that contract. A blank rate is informative: it says the provision was measured with no solved rate behind it.</li><li><b>Discount Status</b> explains each row on the discounted basis, including a floating-rate proxy label and a calculated-horizon proxy label where those apply.</li></ul><h4>To export the results</h4><ol><li>Press <b>Export Report</b>.</li><li>Choose the portfolio and the reporting period.</li><li>Choose <b>Summary</b> for the stage-level totals with exposure, average probability, average loss rate and ECL, or <b>Total Loan Book</b> for a loan-level extract.</li><li>On the loan-level extract, tick the columns you want; the contract identifier is always included.</li><li>Press the download button. The file arrives as a CSV.</li></ol><h4>What happens next</h4><p>These figures are what the dashboard, the IFRS 9 Reports hub and the financial statement disclosure tables read. Nothing is posted to a ledger by the platform; the reports are the evidence a preparer uses to raise the provision journal.</p><h4>Common problems</h4><ul><li><b>The list is empty.</b> No ECL has been calculated for the period and scope in the filters. Clear the filters or run the calculation.</li><li><b>Coverage looks wrong on one loan.</b> Check the stage, the probability and the loss rate on that row before questioning the total; a single mis-staged loan moves a portfolio figure.</li><li><b>Discounted and undiscounted totals differ a lot.</b> That difference is the discounting effect card. A large effect usually means long remaining horizons or high effective rates, both of which are worth confirming.</li></ul>',
            'steps' => [
                'Open ECL Processing, then ECL Calculation.',
                'Choose the measurement basis tab: Discounted ECL or Undiscounted ECL.',
                'Press Show filters and narrow the list by year, month, stage or contract.',
                'Read the three summary cards, then check the amber banner for records that could not be discounted.',
                'Press Export Report, choose Summary or Total Loan Book, and download the CSV.',
            ],
            'images' => [
                'ecl' => 'The ECL results screen with the measurement-basis tabs, summary cards and the loan-level table',
            ],
            'routes' => ['expected-credit-loss.index'],
